  "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"b10c\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"114\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/user_avatar/bnoc.xyz/b10c/48/4_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> b10c:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I\u2019m not sure how easy it is to download files via e.g. <code>wget</code> from Google Drive\u2026</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It seems like rclone has Google Drive support:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://rclone.org/drive/\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/original/1X/2d7aafb43f0ad85c7caaa0d954085f3d852e91e4.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"78B8DE\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://rclone.org/drive/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Rclone</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/361;\"><img src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/fe0ef1e95055ef59dd61748e9fcae09dbb7310e9_2_690x362.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"DEE5E9\" width=\"690\" height=\"362\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://rclone.org/drive/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Google drive</a></h3>\n\n  <p>Rclone docs for Google drive</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>But my read of the docs is that that\u2019s mostly for a single user (I\u2019ve used it successfully that way). Not sure how it could be used for people to download from a public / shared folder though; a quick web search suggests its possible?</p>",
